# binaries
/bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
/dist/
# go
/vendor/
# anacrolix/torrent's default piece-completion cache: created wherever a test
# builds a real torrent.Client without an explicit storage dir (11.5's
# internal/engine/torrent_live_test.go does, deliberately, to exercise gopeed's
# bt.Fetcher against a real swarm) - not something this repo's own code names
# or controls, so ignoring it here is the fix rather than a code change.
# Both names, because the library renamed it: a run of the current pin leaves
# .torrent.db behind, and the older .torrent.bolt.db is kept so an older
# checkout does not start showing one either.
# The -shm/-wal suffixes are SQLite's own side files: the same run that leaves
# the database leaves those two next to it, and ignoring only the database is a
# rule that catches one of the three files it was written for.
*.torrent.bolt.db*
.torrent.db*
# local/tmp
/tmp/
.DS_Store

# node
node_modules/
web/node_modules/

# Wails desktop build output - all ignored except appicon.png, which is the
# actual repo asset gen-appicon.mjs writes there (Wails reads it from this
# exact path at build time), not a build output.
desktop/build/*
!desktop/build/appicon.png
desktop/go.sum

# `wails build`/`wails dev` also write generated JS bindings straight into
# the shared web/ project - regenerated on every build, not source.
web/wailsjs/
web/package.json.md5
# A signing key never belongs in here. mobile/.gitignore already covers *.jks
# for the app; this is the same rule at the root, because the one place a
# keystore actually gets dropped by accident is next to whatever command was
# being run at the time.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
